<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Active vehicle for UMW_Piledriver (WeaponTraitDefs/Blunt/Piledriver.xml), granted via
       WeaponTraitDef.abilityProps — see that trait file for the CompEquippableAbilityReloadable wiring.
       Shaped after Odyssey's EMPPulse (Data/Odyssey/Defs/AbilityDefs/WeaponTraitAbilities.xml): pure
       cooldown, no charges, self-centred explosion. Mundane-kinetic tone (design tenet: a physical
       property of the weapon, not magic) — the head's mass slams the ground and the shockwave that rings
       out is a stun, not a blast. Per EMPPulse's own friendly-fire contract the shockwave is
       INDISCRIMINATE — no faction filter, so allies caught in the radius reel just as hostiles do; the
       only pawn spared is the wielder, who is braced behind the shaft (see excludeCaster below).
       damageDef Stun / damageAmount 4: Core's Stun DamageDef (Defs/DamageDefs/Damages_Stun.xml) inherits
       harmsHealth=false from its StunBase parent, and DamageWorker.Apply gates ALL hit-point damage behind
       dinfo.Def.harmsHealth — so this explosion should not injure anyone it stuns (decompile-verified
       2026-07-24, RimWorld 1.6). The duration itself is believed to follow the vanilla "stun ticks =
       damageAmount * 30" rule (amount 4 -> ~120 ticks, 2s) that Odyssey's own ranged stun sources ride, but
       that formula was NOT independently decompile-verified — §7 of the spec calls for an in-game check of
       both the duration math and the harms-health question before this ships; if Stun turns out to injure
       after all, decide there whether to keep the amount (a slam should plausibly hurt a little) or zero it.

       RADIUS 3.9 (was 2.9; verbProperties.range and explosionRadius below must move together —
       decompile-verified 2026-07-25):
       2.9 was a trap value. The gizmo-hover preview is Command_Ability.GizmoUpdateOnMouseover ->
       VerbProperties.DrawRadiusRing -> GenDraw.DrawRadiusRing, which outlines the EDGE of the discrete
       cell set within the radius (DrawFieldEdges), and every cell of the 5x5 bounding box is within 2.9
       (the (2,2) corner sits at 2.828), so the "ring" degenerated into a filled square. The affected set
       was always a euclidean circle — GenRadial.RadialPattern is sorted by true distance — it just happened
       to be a circle that filled its own bounding box exactly. 3.9 is the next X.9 step (45 cells, cardinal
       reach 2 -> 3, corners at (3,3)/4.243 excluded) so it reads round, and it is exactly one cell further
       out. 3.0 would also reach three cells but admits only 29 of them — a sparse diamond, since it excludes
       everything past the exact-integer ring — so X.9 is what fills the disc, which is why vanilla uses it
       throughout (EMPPulse 4.9; Royalty's BlindingPulse and VertigoPulse are 3.9, so this radius is shipped
       precedent for a control ability). Staying under EMPPulse's 4.9 also keeps UMW_Piledriver's +80
       MarketValue at honest parity with the ranged EMPPulser it is priced against.

       PRESENTATION. The burst was always progressive — Explosion.GetCellAffectTick is
       startTick + (int)(distance * 1.5 / propagationSpeed) and Tick() affects cells in distance order — but
       at the vanilla speed of 1 the outermost cell of this radius lands 5 ticks in, far too fast to see.
       propagationSpeed 0.3 stretches that to 18 ticks (0.30s) of visible outward roll, carrying Stun's own
       per-cell BlastDry fleck with it. 0.3 is vanilla's only shipped value for the field (Core's Vaporize).
       soundExplode is set because otherwise Explosion.PlayExplosionSound falls back to
       damType.soundExplosion, i.e. Explosion_Stun — an inherited default rather than a choice. Both it and
       Explosion_Thump are the SAME recording (Weapon/Artillery/Mortar_Explode_Dry) at different pitches:
       Stun sits at 1.65-1.95, a thin high crack that reads electrical, where Thump is the same dry blast
       dropped about two octaves to 0.40-0.50, which is a heavy mass landing on dirt. Same volume (80), so
       this is purely a tone change. Core-owned, so no MayRequire — note a soundExplode pointing at a DLC
       SoundDef would fail cross-reference resolution for players without that DLC, which rules out
       Biotech's otherwise apt Explosion_MechBandShockwave.
       The overhead ripple is FleckDefs/EarthshakeRipple.xml on the vanilla
       CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget, which for a targetRequired=False ability spawns on the caster
       (Command_Ability.ProcessInput passes ability.pawn) via FleckMaker.AttachedOverlay — despite the name
       that just spawns an ordinary static fleck at the pawn's DrawPos, so it stays ground-anchored. See that
       file for how its 4.8-cell reach and 0.40s life are tuned against the numbers here. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>UMW_Earthshake</defName>
    <label>earthshake</label>
    <description>Slam the weapon's full mass into the ground, sending a stunning shockwave out through the earth. The shock passes under walls and stuns friend and foe alike; only the braced wielder keeps their footing.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Commands/UMW_Earthshake</iconPath>
    <aiCanUse>true</aiCanUse>
    <targetRequired>False</targetRequired>
    <!-- Draws the gap-blocked ring instead of a plain radius ring. AbilityDef.gizmoClass is a plain Type
         field that Ability.GetGizmos passes to Activator.CreateInstance, so this needs no Harmony patch;
         the class falls back to vanilla's ring if the shockwave comp is ever absent. -->
    <gizmoClass>UniqueMeleeWeapons.Command_Ability_GroundShockwave</gizmoClass>
    <cooldownTicksRange>30000</cooldownTicksRange> <!-- 12 hours -->
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <!-- Must match explosionRadius below. DrawRadiusRing reads verb.EffectiveRange, i.e. this field, and
           NOT any comp field, so a mismatch draws a preview that lies about the burst. -->
      <range>3.9</range>
      <!-- drawHighlightWithLineOfSight deliberately ABSENT (unlike RallyingCry.xml, whose comp really does
           require line of sight to each ally). The shock travels through the ground, so it is not
           LOS-filtered at all — but it IS gap-blocked, which no VerbProperties field can express, so the
           ring is drawn by the gizmoClass below instead of by this verb. See travelsThroughGround. -->
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <warmupTime>0.5</warmupTime>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <!-- Our CompProperties_AbilityExplosion subclass (Source/1.6/Abilities/). Identical to the vanilla
           comp except for the three fields at the bottom, each of which vanilla hardcodes with no XML hook;
           that file documents why each one needs the subclass. -->
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.CompProperties_AbilityGroundShockwave">
        <damageDef>Stun</damageDef>
        <explosionRadius>3.9</explosionRadius> <!-- keep verbProperties.range above in step with this -->
        <damageAmount>4</damageAmount> <!-- ~120t / 2s stun via the amount*30 rule; verify in-game, §7 -->
        <soundExplode>Explosion_Thump</soundExplode> <!-- Stun's own sound pitched down; see PRESENTATION above -->
        <propagationSpeed>0.3</propagationSpeed> <!-- 0.30s of visible outward roll; see PRESENTATION above -->
        <excludeCaster>true</excludeCaster> <!-- the wielder is braced for it; everyone else is not -->
        <travelsThroughGround>true</travelsThroughGround> <!-- walls do not stop it; a gap in the floor does -->
      </li>
      <!-- The shock in the air above, reaching a little past the stun. Vanilla comp, our FleckDef. -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget">
        <fleckDef>UMW_EarthshakeRipple</fleckDef>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

</Defs>
